{"title":"2022 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Pigeonhole_Principle)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Pigeonhole Principle)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Pigeonhole_v2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Pigeonhole v2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Intuitive_and_Fast)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Intuitive and Fast)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is a subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/c/93c2f28e0fe33caa12903b864efac1c505bd1e7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{ 1, 2, 3, \\ldots , 25 \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" /> such that the sum of any two (not necessarily distinct) elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is never an element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d7e49ad93a99ed6dcafd1c6acba511a181ab6a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> What is the maximum number of elements <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> may contain?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fdad4e92e92d3fcc67946a27f3cfdddde84eec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 12 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 13 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 14 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 15 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Pigeonhole_Principle.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Pigeonhole_Principle)\">Solution 1 (Pigeonhole Principle)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Pigeonhole Principle)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the largest number in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\nWe categorize numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/d/73d1c24723375dec94e8c0b4cb1b52665146ef1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{ 1, 2, \\ldots , M-1 \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" /> (except <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dd7f04e416c30f58c3e0c7cc869e342d8cb9626.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{M}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"22\" height=\"37\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is even) into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/f/aef48de7d9481d3123238642170e3136743056de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{M-1}{2} \\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"77\" height=\"45\" /> groups, such that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />th group contains two numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/f/26f7b00e581da7e87b58a20d361a1484c34c5083.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M-i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Recall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/1/dc1de65566573b00a1a8811fc13701f4ea142811.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" /> and the sum of two numbers in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, and the sum of numbers in each group above is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, each of the above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/f/aef48de7d9481d3123238642170e3136743056de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{M-1}{2} \\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"77\" height=\"45\" /> groups can have at most one number in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\nTherefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/5/ed523743fbacf1f6cc5c69c96164c992ea6e460d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} |S| &amp; \\leq 1 + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{M-1}{2} \\right\\rfloor \\\\ &amp; \\leq 1 + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{25}{2} \\right\\rfloor \\\\ &amp; = 13. \\end{align*}\" width=\"147\" height=\"113\" />\n</p><p>Next, we construct an instance of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/b/12ba66ab6180765b6f10a251d6904dfad49314c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S| = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/b/4cb8cdb84c27e0930515f822556b57cf2886bfd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\left\\{ 13, 14, \\ldots , 25 \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" />.\nThus, this set is feasible.\nTherefore, the most number of elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/72580965b4e9bb9f05fc9ba15c4f00c851da4b7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Pigeonhole_v2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Pigeonhole_v2)\">Solution 2 (Pigeonhole v2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Pigeonhole v2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We construct a possible subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> elements by including all odd integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, inclusive. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/2592c51e57020c29f296d1203084aa6b2e8e34a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\left\\{ 1, 3, 5, \\cdots , 25 \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" />. The sum of any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> elements is even, and thus cannot be an element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>To show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> cannot have more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> elements, assume for sake of contradiction that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/6700346c51684f23872487f02005b8b60c74d054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S| \\geq 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b3d5528071fdbccfab7ec5bbb8981133274202b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\left\\{ x_1, x_2, \\cdots , x_n \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/a/61af45bc9e10cda0b27be37378725b9c821ae2bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/8/318c7442fb742e2547842b64b10200b8018577a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 &lt; x_2 &lt; \\cdots &lt; x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"15\" />. Because the sums of any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (not necessarily distinct) elements do not appear in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/d/92d27d9d6b1a75f1c322046ec0d612b16aa33c0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1+x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> is not an element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/f/b4fef0a6ea1670d0b47c20aa14ee5b16b42cf183.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq i \\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83c2e7964bc1384b456f82f7b096c59c8cc2554d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2, \\cdots , x_n , x_1+x_1, x_1+x_2, \\cdots , x_1+x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"343\" height=\"16\" /> are all distinct integers. Let these integers be elements of the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/a/cba1f142cd28a4fd9e9f08071bc03d6c9f21ad05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|T|=2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />, and because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/a/61af45bc9e10cda0b27be37378725b9c821ae2bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/2/0620a5e07fdacfe160a82d396df8aad57cf4672f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|T| \\geq 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" />. But all elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/262fc9b6d98ab05e88848a8d55c082d5b73586e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\geq x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/e/43eb2405490c3eed6f8983498bc8761548f95d28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leq x_1+x_n \\leq x_1+25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"17\" />, leaving only 26 possible values for the elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. By the Pigeonhole Principle, the elements cannot be distinct, and we have a contradiction.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/72580965b4e9bb9f05fc9ba15c4f00c851da4b7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" /> is the maximum possible size of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~starwars101\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Intuitive_and_Fast.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Intuitive_and_Fast)\">Solution 3 (Intuitive and Fast)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Intuitive and Fast)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice how \\( 24 + 25 &gt; 25 \\), \\( 23 + 24 &gt; 25 \\), and this continues backward until \\( n + n+1 &gt; 25 \\). We then see that \\( 2n+1 &gt; 25 \\rightarrow 2n &gt; 24 \\rightarrow n &gt; 12 \\).\n</p><p>Thus the elements in the set must have the property \\( n &gt; 12&#160;: n \\in \\mathbb{Z}^+ \\) and therefore our set is \\( \\{13, 14, 15, \\dots, 25\\} \\) in which there is \\( 25 - 13 + 1 \\Rightarrow \\) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/72580965b4e9bb9f05fc9ba15c4f00c851da4b7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" /> elements.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/_K29sOequlY\">https://youtu.be/_K29sOequlY</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/in3N3Os5kGw\">https://youtu.be/in3N3Os5kGw</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Mi2AxPhnRno?t=1056\">https://youtu.be/Mi2AxPhnRno?t=1056</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\">2025 AMC 10A Q21/AMC 12A Q15</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B\">2022 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1